{
  "text": " Conversation 4. Running into a Friend Hi, Jen. What's up? I haven't seen you for ages. Nicole, fancy running into you here. Do you have time for a cup of coffee? Sure. We really need to catch up. Do you work around here? At the dress shop across the street. I'm a sales assistant for the time being, but I'm hoping they'll promote me to buyer after I have some experience on the floor. Oh, I love that shop. Their clothes are so trendy and different from the run-of-the-mill. You look fantastic. I'll bet their sales have gone up since you started working there. Well, I try. The thing is, I enjoy the work because I love the clothes, and I like helping people find what works for them. It's actually quite fulfilling. Good for you. And I think the idea of becoming a buyer is great. Before you know it, you'll be working on your own designs. I remember how you used to dream of being a fashion designer. Yeah, and I think this is a step in the right direction. Now, what are you up to? The last I heard, you were about to move across country. I hope you back to stay As a matter of fact I just got back a couple of months ago I glad I went because now I know I really want to be here I working as a waitress right now but I hoping to get a teaching job. I've applied to most of the local school districts, so I have my fingers crossed I'll get something this fall. What do you want to teach? I've heard there are openings for high school teachers in Howard County. No way. I haven't even applied there. I'll do it as soon as I get home. Man, that'll be awesome if they need a biology teacher. Thanks for the tip. Which reminds me, waiting tables isn't all bad. On weekends, I get pretty good tips. And banking on the info you just gave me, I think I'll follow you back to work and splurge on a new dress. Great. I already have in mind some things for you to try on. Later. Wow, I love this one. I guess I'm getting ahead of myself, but I have a feeling this is just what I need for the interview with the principal. And for the first day of school... Thanks so much for your help. Now I'm really pumped. I'm so happy I ran into you today. Me too. Let's make sure we get together more often. Yeah, I promise I'll keep in touch Take care and let me know what happens Bye for now Bye and thanks again",
